# What must never reach the build context.
#
# The first entry is the one that matters: .env holds GROQ_API_KEY and the Atlas
# connection string. Compose injects those as environment variables at RUN time; baking
# them into an image LAYER would make them readable by anyone who can pull it, and
# deleting the file in a later layer would not remove it from the earlier one.
.env
.env.*

# Build outputs. Copying a host-built target/ in would let a stale jar win over the one
# the Maven stage produces, and node_modules is both huge and platform-specific - a
# Windows-resolved tree is not what node:22-alpine needs.
target/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# Documentation and local scratch. None of it is read by the build, and every file in
# the context is uploaded to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
docs/
*.md
